WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.520 --> 00:00:04.540
Chances are, you probably aren't overly eager
to lock lips with most of the people at your

00:00:04.540 --> 00:00:05.040
job.

00:00:05.060 --> 00:00:09.440
It's really no different for actors, but they
have to do it fairly often, and sometimes,

00:00:09.440 --> 00:00:12.150
the results are as uncomfortable to watch
as they must have been to film.

00:00:13.150 --> 00:00:17.390
While it's a bit weird that a kiss between
two teenage characters would be widely anticipated,

00:00:17.390 --> 00:00:21.040
Harry Potter and the Deathly Hallows Part
2 is a franchise-concluding exception.

00:00:21.190 --> 00:00:25.560
Hermione Granger and Ron Weasley's combative
relationship begins to soften ever so slightly

00:00:25.560 --> 00:00:27.780
once they admit their romantic feelings for
each other.

00:00:27.960 --> 00:00:32.280
After a particularly harrowing series of events
in which their survival is far from assured,

00:00:32.280 --> 00:00:34.240
Hermione and Ron finally lock lips.

00:00:42.100 --> 00:00:45.960
But rather than taking the audience deeper
into this intense moment and the terrifying

00:00:45.960 --> 00:00:50.039
events that preceded it, their kiss is awkward
enough to have the audience looking away.

00:00:50.039 --> 00:00:54.690
Talking to MTV News, Emma Watson confessed
that she and Rupert Grint were extremely uncomfortable

00:00:54.690 --> 00:00:58.900
and nervous during filming, and Watson in
particular since it was her first proper onscreen

00:00:58.900 --> 00:00:59.400
kiss.

00:01:00.420 --> 00:01:03.740
"It was ones the only...it was honestly like
kissing my brother.

00:01:04.380 --> 00:01:04.900
It was weird."

00:01:06.060 --> 00:01:09.500
Silver Linings Playbook garnered a whole host
of awards season attention.

00:01:09.500 --> 00:01:13.369
This quirky drama is about a mentally ill
man named Pat who is forced to move back in

00:01:13.369 --> 00:01:15.380
with his parents after his marriage falls
apart.

00:01:15.520 --> 00:01:19.140
While there, he gets caught up with manic
pixie dream girl Tiffany who manages to rope

00:01:19.140 --> 00:01:21.800
him into being her dance partner for a ballroom
competition.

00:01:21.980 --> 00:01:26.200
While their onscreen smooch did win an MTV
Movie Award for Best Kiss, their saliva swap

00:01:26.200 --> 00:01:28.540
was as awkward to film as it was to watch.

00:01:28.740 --> 00:01:32.140
On The Graham Norton Show, Cooper revealed
that Lawrence called him out on set for being

00:01:32.140 --> 00:01:32.920
a bad kisser:

00:01:33.140 --> 00:01:35.820
"After the second take [Lawrence] said, 'You're
a wet kisser.

00:01:35.829 --> 00:01:36.829
You don't want to hear that.

00:01:36.829 --> 00:01:37.820
It was not a compliment."

00:01:38.560 --> 00:01:42.680
After proposing to his longtime girlfriend
Fat Amy, Bumper is unceremoniously and publicly

00:01:42.680 --> 00:01:46.080
dumped by Amy, who claims she is far from
ready to stop playing the field, even though

00:01:46.080 --> 00:01:49.860
in Pitch Perfect 2 and its predecessor, she's
only been interested in him.

00:01:49.869 --> 00:01:53.630
They spend much of the movie apart until Amy
has an epiphany at a capella boot camp and

00:01:53.630 --> 00:01:57.460
decides she really does love him and now wants
to change her final answer to a resounding

00:01:57.460 --> 00:01:57.980
"yes."

00:01:58.080 --> 00:02:02.280
To the tune of Pat Benatar's We Belong, sung
by Rebel Wilson and Adam DeVine, Bumper and

00:02:02.280 --> 00:02:06.340
Amy reconnect in one of the most awkward kissing
scenes of the past decade, although this one's

00:02:06.340 --> 00:02:07.840
definitely awkward on purpose.

00:02:07.940 --> 00:02:12.000
As they weirdly lip-lock and roll around the
grass while also managing to keep singing,

00:02:12.000 --> 00:02:14.420
the awkwardness just heightens the romantic
comedy ick factor.

00:02:15.240 --> 00:02:19.280
Angelina Jolie is no stranger to being called
out for awkward onscreen kisses, which is

00:02:19.280 --> 00:02:22.980
bizarre considering she's consistently named
one of the world's most beautiful women.

00:02:23.060 --> 00:02:27.780
First it was her uncomfortable and passionless
lip-lock with James McAvoy in 2008's Wanted,

00:02:27.820 --> 00:02:29.780
which was as awkward to film as it was to
watch.

00:02:39.300 --> 00:02:42.959
But this past decade, she and co-star Johnny
Depp get the prize for lackluster kissing

00:02:42.960 --> 00:02:44.780
scenes everyone expected to smolder.

00:02:44.780 --> 00:02:48.900
Instead, their makeout sessions are about
as spicy as a boiled potato, and Depp told

00:02:48.900 --> 00:02:52.260
the Mirror that he was uncomfortable filming
the scenes and had to use humor to get through

00:02:52.260 --> 00:02:52.760
them.

00:02:52.880 --> 00:02:56.600
It just goes to show that just because a movie
casts two gorgeous leads doesn't mean there

00:02:56.600 --> 00:02:57.840
will be onscreen chemistry.

00:02:58.320 --> 00:03:00.180
"What an awkward situation."

00:03:01.460 --> 00:03:05.860
As the dinosaurs take over once again in Jurassic
World, a lot of questionable things go down.

00:03:05.860 --> 00:03:10.830
First, they've made a hybrid dinosaur from
recombinant DNA that is not only majorly aggressive,

00:03:10.830 --> 00:03:14.030
but its chameleon traits allow it to fully
blend into any surroundings.

00:03:14.030 --> 00:03:18.090
Second, as Claire, Owen, and her nephews are
being hunted by dinosaurs, Claire and Owen

00:03:18.090 --> 00:03:21.080
share an awkward lip lock that is completely
out of place.

00:03:30.180 --> 00:03:34.560
Yes, there are indeed times in life when a
well-timed kiss even amid inappropriate circumstances

00:03:34.560 --> 00:03:37.820
can help to relieve tension, whether in real
life or onscreen.

00:03:38.120 --> 00:03:41.300
But the jury is still out on whether this
applies to being under attack from hordes

00:03:41.300 --> 00:03:42.000
of dinosaurs.

00:03:42.240 --> 00:03:46.500
Funnily enough, according to Jurassic World's
leading lady, the kiss was unscripted and

00:03:46.500 --> 00:03:49.720
spontaneous, which only makes it worse that
it came off so awkward.

00:03:50.640 --> 00:03:55.480
Tate Taylor's revenge horror movie Ma features
Octavia Spencer as Sue Ann Ellington, a veterinary

00:03:55.480 --> 00:03:57.280
assistant in a small American town.

00:03:57.360 --> 00:04:00.940
After a group of high school kids headed by
Andy Hawkins asks Sue Ann to buy liquor for

00:04:00.950 --> 00:04:05.150
them, she realizes that these are the children
of her own high school bullies, and she begins

00:04:05.150 --> 00:04:08.720
concocting an elaborate plan to get back at
the people who most badly hurt her.

00:04:09.000 --> 00:04:13.080
As Sue Ann rampages her way through her list
of offenders, she ends up kissing young Andy,

00:04:13.100 --> 00:04:15.640
who is attempting to placate her more violent
impulses.

00:04:15.740 --> 00:04:19.820
Unlike many of the awkward kisses of the last
decade, this scene is orchestrated to creepy

00:04:19.830 --> 00:04:24.220
effect on purpose, highlighting Sue Ann's
post-traumatic psychosis as well as how far

00:04:24.220 --> 00:04:26.020
the teens will go in order to survive.

00:04:26.640 --> 00:04:30.600
The Jennifer Lawrence and Chris Pratt sci-fi
drama Passengers doesn't only feature one

00:04:30.600 --> 00:04:34.450
of the most awkward kissing scenes of the
past decade, it's also arguably one of the

00:04:34.450 --> 00:04:38.479
most uncomfortable movies of the decade to
boot with an incredibly problematic plot.

00:04:38.480 --> 00:04:42.600
Pratt plays Jim, a passenger on a space colony
ship who wakes up decades early during the

00:04:42.600 --> 00:04:43.100
voyage.

00:04:43.180 --> 00:04:47.160
He sees another passenger, Aurora, whom he
falls in love with and decides to wake her

00:04:47.160 --> 00:04:48.520
up so he won't be alone anymore.

00:04:48.780 --> 00:04:52.580
He does this despite the fact that doing so
will doom her to a lonely life and death on

00:04:52.580 --> 00:04:53.520
the ship along with him.

00:04:53.840 --> 00:04:54.340
Yikes.

00:04:54.600 --> 00:04:58.900
It's a while before Aurora finds out her awakening
wasn't an accident like Jim's, at which point

00:04:58.900 --> 00:05:01.740
they've already begun a relationship that
includes physical intimacy.

00:05:01.960 --> 00:05:05.680
Passengers was Jennifer Lawrence's first sex
scene, as well as her first time kissing a

00:05:05.680 --> 00:05:06.600
married co-star.

00:05:06.690 --> 00:05:10.160
She was so uncomfortable with the scenario
that she said she ended up getting drunk to

00:05:10.160 --> 00:05:14.620
film their scenes, which only made the situation
even more awkward to film and to watch.

00:05:16.240 --> 00:05:18.220
"Don't eat that, no…That's not what you..."

00:05:19.100 --> 00:05:22.680
Shailene Woodley isn't only known for her
strong performances in films like the Divergent

00:05:22.680 --> 00:05:24.920
series as well as HBO's Big Little Lies.

00:05:25.200 --> 00:05:29.740
She's also known to be really into holistic
therapies, Chinese medicine, and clean eating.

00:05:29.740 --> 00:05:33.069
You'd think her healthy lifestyle would make
her an optimal kissing partner, but her The

00:05:33.069 --> 00:05:36.180
Spectacular Now co-star Miles Teller has a
different perspective.

00:05:36.180 --> 00:05:37.930
Talking to Variety, Teller recalled,

00:05:37.930 --> 00:05:41.660
"Before our first kissing scene, Shailene
took these Chinese dirt supplements and shoved

00:05:41.660 --> 00:05:42.540
them in her mouth.

00:05:42.669 --> 00:05:46.520
It's like a dirt pouch, and it smells like
crap...She always has a mason jar and 100%

00:05:46.520 --> 00:05:48.140
of the time it smells like crap."

00:05:48.420 --> 00:05:52.120
"I, I had some this morning, so you might
be like, 'Shay, stay away, because you have

00:05:52.120 --> 00:05:53.180
fire dragon breath.'"

00:05:53.750 --> 00:05:57.800
Luckily for Teller, most of their kissing
scenes were in the middle of fraught and complicated

00:05:57.800 --> 00:06:01.320
situations, so he didn't necessarily need
to look like he was fully enjoying things.

00:06:02.100 --> 00:06:06.540
After several bombs, master of the twist ending
M. Night Shyamalan returned in 2016 with the

00:06:06.540 --> 00:06:08.520
multiple personality horror movie Split.

00:06:08.700 --> 00:06:12.840
James McAvoy plays Kevin Wendell Crumb, a
man so traumatized by the abuse he survived

00:06:12.840 --> 00:06:17.240
as a child he has created an entire army of
alternate personalities that help him cope.

00:06:17.240 --> 00:06:20.910
These personalities have begun to merge into
the Horde and the Beast, a violent being who

00:06:20.910 --> 00:06:21.900
defies the laws of nature.

00:06:22.260 --> 00:06:26.180
The Horde has kidnapped three high school
girls, including Casey Cooke, and is keeping

00:06:26.180 --> 00:06:27.860
them prisoner for the Beast's next meal.

00:06:28.080 --> 00:06:31.960
One of Kevin's alters is nine-year-old Hedwig,
who Casey manages to bond with and almost

00:06:31.960 --> 00:06:32.960
allows her to escape.

00:06:32.960 --> 00:06:37.349
In the process, Hedwig asks if he can kiss
Casey, who has no choice but to comply.

00:06:37.349 --> 00:06:41.260
The result is one of the most awkward kisses
ever, let alone the past decade.

00:06:51.580 --> 00:06:55.440
There is still so much that is unclear about
the sixth installment of the Alien franchise.

00:06:55.450 --> 00:06:59.900
Set years after the future events depicted
in Prometheus, Alien: Covenant finds the android

00:06:59.900 --> 00:07:04.160
David after he's fashioned himself a kingdom
on the home planet of humanity's creators,

00:07:04.160 --> 00:07:05.060
called the Engineers.

00:07:05.180 --> 00:07:08.990
David lures a colony ship on their way to
terraform a new planet to his home on Paradise,

00:07:08.990 --> 00:07:12.500
where he meets Walter, a new android model
who looks just like David.

00:07:12.750 --> 00:07:16.720
David shows Walter his creepy lair, covered
in sketches of the Xenomorph creature, jars

00:07:16.720 --> 00:07:20.360
filled with all kinds of weird stuff, and
a variety of tools and instruments that David

00:07:20.360 --> 00:07:22.020
has been creating or repurposing.

00:07:22.220 --> 00:07:25.940
After teaching Walter how to play the flute,
David kisses Walter full on the mouth.

00:07:25.940 --> 00:07:29.910
Why he does this is never explained (maybe
an expression of pure narcissism to kiss his

00:07:29.910 --> 00:07:34.280
identical twin?) but it is as awkward as awkward
gets, made worse by the fact that David tries

00:07:34.280 --> 00:07:36.400
to kill Walter almost immediately after.

00:07:37.080 --> 00:07:40.900
Reese Witherspoon had a decidedly unpleasant
experience on the set of her carnival period

00:07:40.900 --> 00:07:43.680
piece Water for Elephants with co-star Robert
Pattinson.

00:07:43.960 --> 00:07:47.800
This romantic drama stars Pattinson as Jacob,
a veterinary student who drops out of school

00:07:47.800 --> 00:07:49.640
to join the Benzini Brothers Circus.

00:07:49.900 --> 00:07:53.720
There Jacob meets Witherspoon's Marlena and
her abusive partner, the big top ringmaster

00:07:53.720 --> 00:07:54.220
August.

00:07:54.300 --> 00:07:58.220
He can't help but fall in love with this beautiful
but damaged woman even though August's temper

00:07:58.230 --> 00:08:00.729
would put them all in danger if he ever found
out.

00:08:00.729 --> 00:08:04.479
During one of their kissing scenes, the music
swells in elaborate and emotional waves, but

00:08:04.479 --> 00:08:07.540
Pattinson later totally ruined the moment
in an interview with MTV, saying:

00:08:07.540 --> 00:08:09.810
"I was doing it when I had a really bad cold.

00:08:09.810 --> 00:08:13.349
My nose is running all over the place, and
it was in one of the additional photography

00:08:13.349 --> 00:08:17.599
scenes, and Reese had this wig on, and literally,
I was wiping my nose on her wig."

00:08:17.599 --> 00:08:19.020
Witherspoon corroborated his story, saying,

00:08:19.020 --> 00:08:20.860
"He did have a very runny nose, yeah.

00:08:21.020 --> 00:08:22.480
It wasn't appealing; it wasn't pleasant."

00:08:23.380 --> 00:08:26.539
There's nothing like implied incest to make
any situation awkward.

00:08:26.539 --> 00:08:30.720
In We're the Millers, drug dealer David Clark
has to smuggle an RV full of marijuana across

00:08:30.720 --> 00:08:32.900
the border and needs a cover family to help.

00:08:33.000 --> 00:08:36.940
He enlists dancer Sarah Rose to be his pretend
wife, and runaway Casey and his neighbor Kenny

00:08:36.940 --> 00:08:38.280
to round out the fake family.

00:08:38.560 --> 00:08:41.740
On the way they link up with another family,
and Kenny starts crushing on their daughter

00:08:41.740 --> 00:08:42.240
Melissa.

00:08:42.380 --> 00:08:46.280
Kenny wants to make a move but doesn't know
how to kiss, so Casey and Sarah Rose give

00:08:46.280 --> 00:08:47.500
him a detailed tutorial.

00:08:47.830 --> 00:08:51.680
Of course Melissa walks in on them, horrified,
not realizing that these folks aren't actually

00:08:51.680 --> 00:08:52.580
family at all.

00:08:52.680 --> 00:08:53.240
Awkward!

00:08:53.480 --> 00:08:57.980
Since this reveal potentially threatens their
cover story, more hijinks ensue for "The Millers."

00:08:57.980 --> 00:09:01.640
According to actor Will Poulter, the scene
was as awkward to film as it was to watch.

00:09:02.400 --> 00:09:06.660
By the close of Avengers: Endgame, the decades-long
love affair between Captain America, a.k.a.

00:09:06.670 --> 00:09:11.420
Steve Rogers, and Peggy Carter ends up taking
on new prominence as the Avengers undo Thanos'

00:09:11.420 --> 00:09:12.000
murderous snap.

00:09:12.200 --> 00:09:16.280
It was undeniable how much Cap loved Peggy,
but Captain America: Civil War features an

00:09:16.280 --> 00:09:20.290
unintentionally awkward kiss between Cap and
Peggy's great-niece Sharon Carter, which takes

00:09:20.290 --> 00:09:22.620
place after they've both attended Peggy's
funeral.

00:09:22.740 --> 00:09:25.600
Peggy Carter actress Hayley Atwell herself
told Entertainment Weekly,

00:09:25.760 --> 00:09:27.700
"I wouldn't want to date my great aunt's guy.

00:09:27.700 --> 00:09:30.350
It just feels like it crosses an incestuous
boundary.

00:09:30.350 --> 00:09:31.430
And Peggy just died.

00:09:31.430 --> 00:09:33.050
That's even more disrespectful, right?

00:09:33.050 --> 00:09:34.170
It's like, 'Don't touch that.

00:09:34.170 --> 00:09:35.170
You can't tap that!'"

00:09:35.170 --> 00:09:39.320
Not only does Atwell have an excellent point,
Chris Evans and Emily VanCamp also had questionable

00:09:39.320 --> 00:09:43.140
onscreen chemistry that made a problematic
kiss even more awkward to watch.

